> Noisy curve fits

>> Offset-exponential decay: preserve the declared generating model

Use 40 points t=.25*i, y=5*exp(-.7*t)+one plus normal noise SD .1, seed 42.
The native data recipe owns a local mt19937_64; standard normal distribution
implementations can differ across platforms. The parameter order is (A,k,c), with
residual A*exp(-k*t)+c-y and Jacobian row (exp(-k*t),-A*t*exp(-k*t),one).
Start at (1,.1,0), use default damping and a 200-step budget, and check the
analytic Jacobian separately using scale-aware central differences. That check
has truncation and rounding error; it is not the derivative used by the optimizer.
Known generating parameters describe the simulation, not the exact optimum of
a noisy sample. Training RMSE or small gradient does not certify model adequacy
or out-of-sample prediction uncertainty.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/opt_lm_exponential.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace o           = dm::optim;
  const auto       data = o::optimization_curve_data("exponential_offset", 40, 42);
  o::CurveResidual f(data, "exponential_offset");
  const auto run = o::trace_optimize<o::ResidualFunction>(f, o::LevenbergMarquardt(), {1, .1, 0});
  const auto x   = data.numeric_column("x").values();
  auto       fit =
      dm::graphics::RPlot::create()
          .points(x, data.numeric_column("y").values(), "observed", {130, 130, 130}, 3)
          .line(x, data.numeric_column("truth").values(), "generating mean", {190, 100, 35})
          .line(x, f.predict(run.coordinates), "LM fit", {40, 100, 190})
          .title("Offset-exponential decay")
          .x_label("time")
          .y_label("response")
          .x_limits(0, 9.75)
          .y_limits(0, 8)
          .legend({"observed", "mean", "fit"}, {{130, 130, 130}, {190, 100, 35}, {40, 100, 190}});
  const auto          v = run.trace.values();
  std::vector<double> logloss;
  for (double z : v.numeric_column("value").values())
    logloss.push_back(std::log10(std::max(1e-14, z)));
  auto trials =
      dm::graphics::RPlot::create()
          .line(
              v.numeric_column("event").values(), logloss, "all residual requests", {40, 100, 190})
          .title("Trial losses, including rejected steps")
          .x_label("callback request index")
          .y_label("log10 half SSE");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2).add(fit).add(trials).size(1100, 490).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/opt_lm_exponential.svg");
  std::print(
      "{}\n\nJ-transpose-r norm: {:.8g}; training residual RMSE: {:.8g}.\n\n{}\n",
      run.summary().to_md(8),
      o::residual_gradient_norm(f, run.coordinates),
      std::sqrt(2 * run.checked_value / data.nrows()),
      o::check_residual_jacobian(f, {4.2, .6, .8}).to_md(10));
}
```
