>> Logistic growth: a different residual geometry

Use 50 points t=.2*i, true (L,k,mid)=(10,1.5,5), normal noise SD .15 and seed 43.
For p=logistic(k*(t-mid)), the Jacobian row is
(p,L*(t-mid)*p*(1-p),-L*k*p*(1-p)). Stable logistic evaluation prevents avoidable
exponential overflow in the inverse link, but does not solve parameter-identifiability
or local-optimum problems. The deliberately poor start remains (1,.1,0). The same
half-SSE convention, proposed-step caveat and independent derivative checks apply.
No real dataset is forced: the original generated curves provide known means and
exact derivative formulas for checking this optimizer.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/opt_lm_logistic.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace o           = dm::optim;
  const auto       data = o::optimization_curve_data("logistic", 50, 43);
  o::CurveResidual f(data, "logistic");
  const auto run = o::trace_optimize<o::ResidualFunction>(f, o::LevenbergMarquardt(), {1, .1, 0});
  const auto x   = data.numeric_column("x").values();
  auto       fit =
      dm::graphics::RPlot::create()
          .points(x, data.numeric_column("y").values(), "observed", {130, 130, 130}, 3)
          .line(x, data.numeric_column("truth").values(), "generating mean", {190, 100, 35})
          .line(x, f.predict(run.coordinates), "LM fit", {40, 100, 190})
          .title("Logistic growth")
          .x_label("time")
          .y_label("response")
          .x_limits(0, 9.8)
          .y_limits(-.5, 14)
          .legend({"observed", "mean", "fit"}, {{130, 130, 130}, {190, 100, 35}, {40, 100, 190}});
  const auto          v = run.trace.values();
  std::vector<double> logloss;
  for (double z : v.numeric_column("value").values())
    logloss.push_back(std::log10(std::max(1e-14, z)));
  auto trials =
      dm::graphics::RPlot::create()
          .line(
              v.numeric_column("event").values(), logloss, "all residual requests", {40, 100, 190})
          .title("Trial losses, including rejected steps")
          .x_label("callback request index")
          .y_label("log10 half SSE");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2).add(fit).add(trials).size(1100, 490).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/opt_lm_logistic.svg");
  std::print(
      "{}\n\nJ-transpose-r norm: {:.8g}; training residual RMSE: {:.8g}.\n\n{}\n",
      run.summary().to_md(8),
      o::residual_gradient_norm(f, run.coordinates),
      std::sqrt(2 * run.checked_value / data.nrows()),
      o::check_residual_jacobian(f, {9, 1.2, 4.5}).to_md(10));
}
```
