>> A tiny rejected proposal is not a stationarity certificate

Return to the constant-curve control and compare initial damping .001, one and
1e20. At 1e20, the first amplitude proposal is only about 4e-20. Its loss rounds
to the unchanged value five, so the strict-decrease test rejects it; the tiny-step
test then ends the solve. The returned amplitude stays zero and J transpose r has
norm four. This is an exact mechanism for premature stopping under excessive
damping, rather than evidence that the residuals were minimised.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/opt_lm_overdamping.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace o = dm::optim;
  dm::dstruct::DataFrame data;
  data.add_column("x", std::vector<double>{0, 0});
  data.add_column("y", std::vector<double>{1, 3});
  o::CurveResidual                     f(data);
  const std::vector<std::string>       labels{"mu .001", "mu 1", "mu 1e20"};
  const std::vector<dm::graphics::RGB> colors{{40, 100, 190}, {190, 100, 35}, {140, 75, 160}};
  auto                                 plot  = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  std::size_t                          index = 0;
  for (double damping : {.001, 1., 1e20}) {
    o::LevenbergMarquardtOptions opt;
    opt.initial_damping = damping;
    const auto run = o::trace_optimize<o::ResidualFunction>(f, o::LevenbergMarquardt(opt), {0, 0});
    const auto v   = run.trace.values();
    plot.line(
        v.numeric_column("event").values(),
        v.numeric_column("value").values(),
        labels[index],
        colors[index]);
    std::print(
        "{}\n\n{}\n\nFinal J-transpose-r norm: {:.8g}.\n\n",
        labels[index],
        run.summary().to_md(8),
        o::residual_gradient_norm(f, run.coordinates));
    ++index;
  }
  plot.title("Overdamping and proposed-step stopping")
      .x_label("callback request index")
      .y_label("half residual SSE")
      .y_limits(.8, 7.5)
      .abline_h(1, {130, 130, 130}, 1)
      .legend(labels, colors)
      .size(850, 490)
      .save_svg("build/opt_lm_overdamping.svg");
}
```
